--
N5008 [class.virtual]/2: D::f overrides A::f in both of D's A subobjects;
a call through the A of C enters D::f with `this' adjusted from that
subobject to D (Itanium C++ ABI 2.5: a thunk in the secondary virtual
table), so D::f reads both A::i.  The front end rejected the class.  g++ 13
and clang++ 18 accept this program, and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
